theory.intro:
A quadrilateral has a line of symmetry if it can be folded so the two halves match exactly. It has rotational symmetry if it looks the same when turned about its centre.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(3,0)--(2.4,1.8)--(0.6,1.8)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1.5,-0.4)--(1.5,2.2);
\node[font=\small] at (1.5,-0.8) {fold line};
\draw (4.5,0)--(7.5,0)--(8.1,1.8)--(5.1,1.8)--cycle;
\fill (6.3,0.9) circle (2pt);
\draw[->] (6.85,0.9) arc (0:280:0.55);
\node[font=\small] at (6.3,-0.8) {turn about the centre};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
A non-square rectangle has a vertical midline and diagonal $AC$ drawn.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.75,every node/.style={font=\normalsize,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0) rectangle (4.8,2.6);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,0)--(4.8,2.6);
\draw[black,dashed] (2.4,-0.3)--(2.4,2.9);
\node[below left] at (0,0) {$A$}; \node[above right] at (4.8,2.6) {$C$};
\node[above] at (2.4,2.9) {midline};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Which drawn line is a line of symmetry? Explain using a fold.
(b) State the total number of lines of symmetry.

foundation.question_text:
How many lines of symmetry does this square have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many lines of symmetry does this non-square rectangle have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.5,2.5);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many lines of symmetry does this non-square rhombus have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,-1.8) -- (2.8,0) -- (0,1.8) -- (-2.8,0) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many lines of symmetry does this kite have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,-2.2) -- (1.7,0.6) -- (0,2.2) -- (-1.7,0.6) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many lines of symmetry does this general parallelogram have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) -- (4,0) -- (5.2,2.4) -- (1.2,2.4) -- cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What is the order of rotational symmetry of this non-square rectangle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0) rectangle (4.8,2.2);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

